      "id": 1,
      "text": "La Crescent was founded in 1851 by Peter and Emma Cameron, who named it 'Camerons'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Crescent%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "La Crescent earned the title 'Apple Capital of Minnesota' after Harris planted the first hardy apple trees there in 1857.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25,
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Crescent%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "La Crescent sits on three scenic byways: the Apple Blossom Scenic Byway, National Historic Bluff Country Scenic Byway, and the Great River Road.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.explorelacrescent.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "La Crescent lies on the west bank of the Mississippi River, surrounded by bluffs that offer sweeping river views and abundant wildlife.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Crescent%2C_Minnesota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Peter Cameron tried to dig a canal to redirect the Mississippi past La Crescent, but he died before its completion; the unfinished canal still shows in aerial photos.",
